Differential fuzzing of --seam on programs with objects (utils/fuzz-seam.py; not
an oracle). A-INB is assumed and reported, not discharged. Accesses at object
bases, and cells (many numeral cells of several objects, every access inside
its object, memory read back by the assertion): A-INB holds, so every variant
(--seam, --seam-arm=0, --seam-store-map=0, --seam-inb=0) agrees with plain and
no run falls back to no A-INB; for cells Store-Map fires and the final run
reports rules that need A-INB (smap.commute, cross-base skips). Violating
modes (accesses anywhere, cells-violate, circular, ptrmem): plain and
--seam-inb=0 agree, --seam may differ (seam-differs: its answer is conditional
on A-INB); when --seam is unsat and plain is sat, the counterexample of plain
is run by sea-run on the abstract program and must make an access outside its
object (oob-confirmed). Circular: the shape of the A-INB circularity (a
load-dependent assume / branch / address after a store through another
object's offset): seed 0, n=12 has 3 programs on which --seam is unsat and
plain sat, each confirmed out of bounds (the shape on which a solver check
built from the A-INB encoding gave a wrong "A-INB holds"). Ptrmem: a pointer
stored in memory and reloaded after a store that only A-INB lets the rewriting
skip. Cells-violate: the sure violation (numeral offset) is detected statically
in every program (fallbacks).
RUN: %python %sea_src_root/utils/fuzz-seam.py --sea-vc sea-vc %if !yices %{ --solver=z3 %} --seed 1 -n 20 --accesses=bases | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=INB
RUN: %python %sea_src_root/utils/fuzz-seam.py --sea-vc sea-vc %if !yices %{ --solver=z3 %} --seed 2 -n 20 --accesses=any | FileCheck %s
RUN: %python %sea_src_root/utils/fuzz-seam.py --sea-vc sea-vc %if !yices %{ --solver=z3 %} --seed 3 -n 8 --accesses=cells | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CELLS
RUN: %python %sea_src_root/utils/fuzz-seam.py --sea-vc sea-vc %if !yices %{ --solver=z3 %} --seed 4 -n 6 --accesses=cells-violate | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=VIOL
RUN: %python %sea_src_root/utils/fuzz-seam.py --sea-vc sea-vc %if !yices %{ --solver=z3 %} --seed 0 -n 12 --accesses=circular | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CIRC
RUN: %python %sea_src_root/utils/fuzz-seam.py --sea-vc sea-vc %if !yices %{ --solver=z3 %} --seed 1 -n 12 --accesses=ptrmem | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PTRMEM
CHECK: failures: 0
INB: fallbacks: 0
INB: failures: 0
CELLS: smap-fired: {{[1-9][0-9]*}}
CELLS: smap.commute: {{[1-9][0-9]*}}
CELLS: cross-base-skips: {{[1-9][0-9]*}}
CELLS: fallbacks: 0
CELLS: failures: 0
VIOL: fallbacks: 6
VIOL: failures: 0
CIRC: seam-differs: 3
CIRC: oob-confirmed: 3
CIRC: oob-undetermined: 0
CIRC: failures: 0
PTRMEM: oob-confirmed: {{[1-9][0-9]*}}
PTRMEM: failures: 0

